# Part 10f (ADR-0337, ADR-0395, ADR-0387 item 4) in a terminal window, on the tour's image: a refusal of a
# running program is shown on the window's status row, System+G opens the grant line (the row says
# `give vi:`), `+r other.txt` gives that one file to that one `vi`, and the editor reads it; a second `vi`
# is refused again (nothing was stored); System+K offers to kill the line and Enter does. The row is the
# line below the grid: `status TEXT` reads it. A big display has fewer than 24 rows, so no step depends on
# the rows. A grant needs half a second between the key and Enter (the guard), so each is typed after one.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
chord ctrl l
top ~> _
type echo secret > other.txt\r
type echo mine > notes.txt\r
# 1. The refusal is on the row at once, and `vi` is given one file only.
type vi notes.txt\r
pause 1500
status -
type :e! other.txt\r
pause 1000
status vi was not given ~/other.txt (to read)
shot grant-refused
# 2. System+G opens the line; the field is the shell's, so the program sees none of it.
chord meta g
status give vi:
type +r other.txt
pause 800
status give vi: +r other.txt
shot grant-line
type \r
status given until vi ends: +r ~/other.txt
# 3. The file is there now.
type :e! other.txt\r
pause 1000
window
screen secret
# 4. Not stored: a second vi is refused the same file again.
type :q!\r
pause 800
window
screen ~> _
type vi notes.txt\r
pause 1500
status -
type :e! other.txt\r
pause 1000
status vi was not given ~/other.txt (to read)
# 5. A variable gives nothing; a path the shell holds and cannot find is said not to exist (a path outside what
# it holds is refused first, as "this shell does not hold it", before anything is looked up: nothing leaks).
chord meta g
pause 800
type +r $HOME/x
type \r
status $HOME/x: only plain words are given
chord meta g
pause 800
type +r /nowhere
type \r
status /nowhere: does not exist
# 6. The kill offer: Escape keeps, Enter ends the line.
chord meta k
status kill vi? Enter kills, Escape keeps
key esc
status -
chord meta k
pause 800
key ret
pause 1500
window
screen ~> _
type poweroff\r
exit
